#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:12
msgid ""
"Sometimes you need to visualize what your robot is sensing and planning to "
"better develop, test, and debug your system. This article summarizes the ROS "
"developer tools and guidance available to help with visualization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:28
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:31
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:33
msgid ""
"Understanding what a robot is sensing, experiencing, and planning makes "
"development and debugging much easier. Visualization tools in ROS help you "
"convert raw robot data into clear, human-readable visual formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:37
msgid "Core ROS packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:39
msgid ""
":doc:`RViz <Visualization/RViz/RViz-User-Guide/RViz-User-Guide>`: Provides a "
"3D visualization of the robot's perspective, including sensor data and "
"intentions. See `rviz <https://github.com/ros2/rviz>`__ and `rviz default "
"plugins <https://github.com/ros2/rviz/tree/rolling/rviz_default_plugins>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:42
msgid ""
":doc:`rqt <Visualization/About-RQt>`: Plugin-based framework for the ROS "
"integrated graphical user interface. See `rqt_gui and dependent packages "
"<https://index.ros.org/p/rqt_gui/#rolling-deps>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:46
msgid "Community-contributed packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:48
msgid ""
"`Foxglove <https://foxglove.dev/>`__: A collection of tools for visualizing "
"and debugging robot data throughout the development lifecycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-visualization.rst:50
msgid ""
"`Rerun <https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun>`__: Tool to visualize, query, and "
"debug data from robotics, computer vision, and physical AI systems."
msgstr ""
